Subject: Revert "virtio_mmio: disable IRQ wake before free_irq"
Origin: vendor, https://github.com/docker/nerdbox-internal/blob/d0a785911710372d8fc1e0a54ffc4e57255d33da/kernel/patches/6.12.114/0011-Revert-virtio_mmio-disable-IRQ-wake-before-free_irq.patch
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/gregkh/linux 85d82e0d7c2dfd3e75d34f35b7ebbf41f45c9c4e
Drop-When: never: carried for as long as 0012-Revert-virtio-mmio-Remove-virtqueue-list-from-mmio-d.patch, which reverts 8e360ffa4aa6, the commit that cba897b7da47 was built on

From ec7b3047fa3855c68c72a223da7ee8678d6261c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaushik Gnanaskandan <kaushik.gnanaskandan@docker.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:30:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] Revert "virtio_mmio: disable IRQ wake before free_irq"

This reverts commit cba897b7da47befe61cdc1be91186bb4c878a260
(upstream d14d693adb055e98ca705822ba6daebc18602d9a).

Stable took this commit into 6.12.112 together with 8e360ffa4aa6
("virtio-mmio: Remove virtqueue list from mmio device"), which it is
built on. The next patch reverts 8e360ffa4aa6 because it slows down
every Firecracker snapshot restore, and this one has to come out first.

Basically, what we give up is the disable_irq_wake() call in
vm_del_vqs(). It only runs when the device tree marks the virtio-mmio IRQ
as "wakeup-source".
Firecracker never sets that property. On arm64 its virtio-mmio nodes
carry only dma-coherent, compatible, reg, interrupts and
interrupt-parent, and on x86 the devices come from the kernel command
line with no device tree at all.

Link: https://github.com/docker/nerdbox-internal/issues/460
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_mmio.c | 16 +++-------------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_mmio.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_mmio.c
index f420fb5..22fdc6b 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_mmio.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_mmio.c
@@ -87,9 +87,6 @@ struct virtio_mmio_device {
 
 	void __iomem *base;
 	unsigned long version;
-
-	/* True if enable_irq_wake() succeeded for the shared IRQ. */
-	bool wake_irq_enabled;
 };
 
 /* Configuration interface */
@@ -332,17 +329,11 @@ static void vm_del_vqs(struct virtio_device *vdev)
 {
 	struct virtio_mmio_device *vm_dev = to_virtio_mmio_device(vdev);
 	struct virtqueue *vq, *n;
-	int irq = platform_get_irq(vm_dev->pdev, 0);
 
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(vq, n, &vdev->vqs, list)
 		vm_del_vq(vq);
 
-	if (vm_dev->wake_irq_enabled) {
-		disable_irq_wake(irq);
-		vm_dev->wake_irq_enabled = false;
-	}
-
-	free_irq(irq, vm_dev);
+	free_irq(platform_get_irq(vm_dev->pdev, 0), vm_dev);
 }
 
 static void vm_synchronize_cbs(struct virtio_device *vdev)
@@ -469,9 +460,8 @@ static int vm_find_vqs(struct virtio_device *vdev, unsigned int nvqs,
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	if (of_property_read_bool(vm_dev->pdev->dev.of_node, "wakeup-source") &&
-	    !enable_irq_wake(irq))
-		vm_dev->wake_irq_enabled = true;
+	if (of_property_read_bool(vm_dev->pdev->dev.of_node, "wakeup-source"))
+		enable_irq_wake(irq);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < nvqs; ++i) {
 		struct virtqueue_info *vqi = &vqs_info[i];
-- 
